on":"Includes: Blazor, Razor Components","archived_at":null,"archived_by":null}],"state":"closed","locked":false,"assignees":[{"login":"dariatiurina","id":110841893,"node_id":"U_kgDOBptQJQ","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/110841893?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/dariatiurina","html_url":"https://github.com/dariatiurina","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dariatiurina/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dariatiurina/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dariatiurina/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dariatiurina/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dariatiurina/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dariatiurina/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dariatiurina/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dariatiurina/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dariatiurina/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false}],"milestone":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dotnet/aspnetcore/milestones/381","html_url":"https://github.com/dotnet/aspnetcore/milestone/381","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dotnet/aspnetcore/milestones/381/labels","id":14553381,"node_id":"MI_kwDOAQzde84A3hEl","number":381,"title":"11.0-preview5","description":"","creator":{"login":"danroth27","id":1874516,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE4NzQ1MTY=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1874516?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/danroth27","html_url":"https://github.com/danroth27","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/danroth27/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/danroth27/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/danroth27/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/danroth27/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/danroth27/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/danroth27/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/danroth27/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/danroth27/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/danroth27/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"open_issues":0,"closed_issues":171,"state":"closed","created_at":"2026-01-15T18:27:16Z","updated_at":"2026-08-26T07:27:43Z","due_on":"2026-06-09T00:00:00Z","closed_at":"2026-06-10T10:11:40Z"},"comments":4,"created_at":"2026-02-17T13:21:47Z","updated_at":"2026-09-29T09:43:54Z","closed_at":"2026-05-05T13:21:08Z","assignee":{"login":"dariatiurina","id":110841893,"node_id":"U_kgDOBptQJQ","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/110841893?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/dariatiurina","html_url":"https://github.com/dariatiurina","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dariatiurina/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dariatiurina/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dariatiurina/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dariatiurina/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dariatiurina/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dariatiurina/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dariatiurina/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dariatiurina/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dariatiurina/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"draft":false,"pull_request":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dotnet/aspnetcore/pulls/65451","html_url":"https://github.com/dotnet/aspnetcore/pull/65451","diff_url":"https://github.com/dotnet/aspnetcore/pull/65451.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/dotnet/aspnetcore/pull/65451.patch","merged_at":"2026-05-05T13:21:08Z"},"body":"# QuickGrid SSR support\r\n\r\n## Description\r\n\r\n`QuickGrid`'s `Paginator` and column sorting currently require interactivity because they rely on `@onclick` event handlers and in-memory state, which don't work with the `StaticHtmlRenderer`. Page index and sort state are stored in memory, so they're lost between SSR requests and can't be shared via URL.\r\n\r\nThis PR adds URL-driven sorting and pagination to `QuickGrid` so that URL feature work without interactivity (SSR) by persisting state in the URL query string. When the feature is enabled, sortable headers and paginator controls render as `<a>` links so they continue to work without a JavaScript runtime. The feature is controlled by an `AppContext` switch and is **enabled by default**. When feature is disabled, SSR is not supported, but the navigation is also based off URL.\r\n\r\n## Problem\r\n\r\nThere were three main blockers preventing `QuickGrid` from working fully in SSR:\r\n\r\n1. **`@onclick` is not supported in SSR** — The `StaticHtmlRenderer` does not render event handler attributes like `@onclick`, so the pagination buttons and sort column headers had no effect.\r\n2. **In-memory page state** — `PaginationState` stores the current page index in memory, which is lost between SSR requests. Users also cannot share URLs pointing to a specific page.\r\n3. **In-memory sort state** — The current sort column and direction are stored in memory on `QuickGrid`, which is also lost between SSR requests.\r\n\r\n## Considered solutions\r\n\r\n- `Session` / `TempData` — Persist state server-side, keeping public APIs unchanged. Discarded, because it still doesn't allow URL sharing between users.\r\n- **Query string parameters** — Persist state in the URL as `?page=N`, `?sort=ColumnTitle`, `?order=asc/desc`. This option was chosen because it provides a familiar UX, enables link sharing, and works with both SSR and interactive rendering.\r\n\r\n## Feature flag\r\n\r\nThe URL-based navigation behavior is controlled by an `AppContext` switch:\r\n\r\n```\r\nMicrosoft.AspNetCore.Components.QuickGrid.EnableUrlBasedQuickGridNavigationAndSorting\r\n```\r\n\r\n- **Enabled by default** (`true`) — sortable column headers and paginator controls render as `<a>` links with URL query parameters.\r\n- **Opt-out** — set the switch to `false` to render the previous `<button>`-based UI with `@onclick` handlers.\r\n\r\nNote: regardless of the flag, `QuickGrid` and `Paginator` always read sort/page state from the URL query string at startup, subscribe to `NavigationManager.LocationChanged`, and update the URL when the user sorts or paginates. The flag only controls **the rendered HTML element** (anchor vs. button). This is asserted by `QuickGridInteractiveCompatTest`, which verifies that the URL still updates (`sort=...`, `order=...`, `page=...`) even when buttons are rendered.\r\n\r\n## Implemented changes\r\n\r\n### QuickGrid (`QuickGrid.razor.cs`)\r\n\r\n- **New `QueryParameterNamePrefix` parameter** (`[Parameter]`, defaults to `\"\"`) — specifies a prefix for query string parameter names used to persist pagination and sort state. When empty, parameters are named `page`, `sort`, and `order`. When set (e.g., `\"products\"`), parameters become `products_page`, `products_sort`, and `products_order`. This allows multiple grids on the same page without URL parameter conflicts.\r\n- **`NavigationManager` injection** — used to read the current URL and navigate with updated query parameters.\r\n- **`QueryParameterValueSupplier`** — used to parse query string values from the current URL.\r\n- **`OnInitialized`** — parses the initial URL query string and subscribes to `NavigationManager.LocationChanged` to react to URL changes (e.g., browser back/forward).\r\n- **`OnParametersSetAsync`** — propagates the page query parameter name to the associated `PaginationState` so the `Paginator` uses the correct parameter name.\r\n- **`ReadSortFromQueryString()`** — parses `?sort=ColumnTitle&order=asc` from the URL using `QueryParameterValueSupplier` and caches the result for use during column collection. The sort column is identified by its `Title` property.\r\n- **`GetSortUrl()` / `GetSortQueryStringUrl()`** — generates URLs with updated sort query parameters using `NavigationManager.GetUriWithQueryParameters()`.\r\n- **`OnLocationChanged`** — responds to external URL changes (back/forward navigation) by re-reading sort state and refreshing data. Falls back to the default sort column/direction when sort parameters are removed from the URL.\r\n- **Default sort tracking** — stores the initial default sort column and direction (`_defaultSortColumn`, `_defaultSortAscending`) so that removing sort params from the URL restores the original sort order.\r\n- **`SortByColumnAsync`** — now navigates to the new sort URL via `NavigationManager.NavigateTo` (instead of just calling `StateHasChanged()`); this happens regardless of the feature flag, so the URL reflects the current sort even in button-mode.\r\n- **`DisposeAsync`** — updated to unsubscribe from `LocationChanged`.\r\n\r\n### Column sorting (`ColumnBase.razor` / `ColumnBase.razor.css`)\r\n\r\n- **Conditional rendering based on feature flag** — when `EnableUrlBasedQuickGridNavigationAndSorting` is enabled and the column has a non-null `Title`, sortable column headers render as `<a>` elements with an `href` pointing to a URL with updated sort query parameters (via `Grid.GetSortUrl(this)`). When the flag is disabled, the previous `<button>` with `@onclick` is rendered. Columns with a null `Title` fall back to a plain `<div>` (no clickable element).\r\n- **CSS updated** — added `a.col-title` selectors alongside existing `button.col-title`, with `text-decoration: none` and `color: inherit` for link styling consistency.\r\n\r\n### Paginator rendering (`Paginator.razor` / `Paginator.razor.css`)\r\n\r\n- **Conditional rendering based on feature flag** — when enabled, pagination navigation uses `<a>` elements with `href` pointing to the URL for the target page. Disabled state uses `aria-disabled=\"true\"` and `pointer-events: none`. When the flag is disabled, the previous `<button>` with `@onclick` and the `disabled` attribute is rendered.\r\n- **CSS updated** — added `nav a` selectors alongside existing `nav button`, with `aria-disabled` selectors added alongside `:disabled`.\r\n\r\n### Paginator logic (`Paginator.razor.cs`)\r\n\r\n- **`NavigationManager` injection** — used to generate page URLs via `GetUriWithQueryParameter()`.\r\n- **`QueryParameterValueSupplier`** — used to parse the current page from the URL query string.\r\n- **`OnInitialized`** — subscribes to `NavigationManager.LocationChanged`.\r\n- **`OnParametersSet` → `OnParametersSetAsync`** — changed to async so it can read the query string on first render and call `State.SetCurrentPageIndexAsync` if the URL specifies a page that differs from the current state.\r\n- **`ReadPageIndexFromQueryString()`** — parses the 1-based page number from the URL and converts it to a 0-based index. Invalid or non-positive values fall back to page 1.\r\n- **`GoToPageAsync`** — now navigates via `NavigationManager.NavigateTo(GetPageUrl(pageIndex))` instead of directly mutating state. State is updated through the resulting `LocationChanged` flow.\r\n- **`GetPageUrl()`** — generates URLs for pagination links. Page 1 omits the query parameter (clean URL); other pages use `?page=N` (1-based).\r\n- **`OnLocationChanged`** — responds to URL changes by re-reading page state and updating accordingly.\r\n- **`Dispose`** — unsubscribes from `LocationChanged`.\r\n\r\n### PaginationState (`PaginationState.cs`)\r\n\r\n- **`QueryName` internal property** — set by `QuickGrid` so the `Paginator` reads the correct query parameter name (e.g., `page` or `products_page`).\r\n\r\n### Feature flag (`QuickGridFeatureFlags.cs`)\r\n\r\n- New internal static class that reads the `Microsoft.AspNetCore.Components.QuickGrid.EnableUrlBasedQuickGridNavigationAndSorting` `AppContext` switch. Defaults to `true` (enabled) when the switch is not set.\r\n\r\n### Shared infrastructure changes\r\n\r\n- **Moved to shared source** — `QueryParameterValueSupplier.cs`, `QueryParameterNameComparer.cs`, `StringSegmentAccumulator.cs`, and `UrlValueConstraint.cs` moved from `Components/src/Routing/` to `Components/Shared/src/` so they can be consumed by both the `Components` project and `QuickGrid`.\r\n- **`QueryParameterValueSupplier.GetQueryString()`** — new public static method that extracts the query string portion from a URL. Previously a local static method in `SupplyParameterFromQueryValueProvider`, now shared.\r\n- **`QueryStringEnumerable.cs`** — added as a shared source compile include in the QuickGrid project.\r\n\r\n### Project references\r\n\r\n- **`Microsoft.AspNetCore.Components.csproj`** — added shared source includes for the moved routing files.\r\n- **`Microsoft.AspNetCore.Components.QuickGrid.csproj`** — added shared source includes for `QueryParameterValueSupplier`, `QueryParameterNameComparer`, `StringSegmentAccumulator`, `UrlValueConstraint`, and `QueryStringEnumerable`.\r\n\r\n### Public API changes (`PublicAPI.Unshipped.txt`)\r\n\r\n```\r\n+Microsoft.AspNetCore.Components.QuickGrid.QuickGrid<TGridItem>.QueryParameterNamePrefix.get -> string!\r\n+Microsoft.AspNetCore.Components.QuickGrid.QuickGrid<TGridItem>.QueryParameterNamePrefix.set -> void\r\n+override Microsoft.AspNetCore.Components.QuickGrid.Paginator.OnInitialized() -> void\r\n+override Microsoft.AspNetCore.Components.QuickGrid.Paginator.OnParametersSetAsync() -> System.Threading.Tasks.Task!\r\n+override Microsoft.AspNetCore.Components.QuickGrid.QuickGrid<TGridItem>.OnInitialized() -> void\r\n*REMOVED*override Microsoft.AspNetCore.Components.QuickGrid.Paginator.OnParametersSet() -> void\r\n```\r\n\r\n(`OnRowClick` getter/setter entries also appear in the diff but were already added in a prior change.)\r\n\r\n### Tests\r\n\r\n- **`QuickGridNoInteractivityTest`** — E2E tests for SSR (no interactivity) scenarios: paginator display, navigation, link-based pagination, disabled state via `aria-disabled`, sorting by various types, multi-grid independence with `QueryParameterNamePrefix`, dual paginators, out-of-range/invalid page handling, and direct URL loading with sort/page parameters.\r\n- **`QuickGridInteractiveTest`** — E2E tests for interactive server rendering: anchor-based sorting and pagination with URL query parameter verification, dual paginators syncing, and multi-grid independence with prefixed query parameters.\r\n- **`QuickGridInteractiveCompatTest`** — E2E tests for the opt-out path (feature flag disabled via `--DisableUrlDrivenNavigation=true`): verifies button-based sorting and pagination still work, and confirms that the URL **does** still update with sort/page parameters in button-mode.\r\n- **`QuickGridTest`** — removed the legacy in-memory sort and \"items per page\" tests that were superseded by the new SSR/interactive E2E suites.\r\n- **`GridRaceConditionTest`** — updated to register a `TestNavigationManager` in the test service provider (now required by `QuickGrid` and `Paginator`).\r\n- **Test assets** — new `QuickGridComponent.razor` (SSR page with three grids and multiple paginators), `QuickGridInteractive.razor` (interactive server page), and `QuickGridDualPaginatorComponent.razor` (dual paginator test component).\r\n\r\n## Breaking change\r\n\r\nWhen the feature flag is enabled (the default), sort column headers and paginator buttons change from `<button>` elements to `<a>` (link) elements. Any custom CSS targeting `button.col-title` or `nav button` in the paginator will need to be updated to also target `a.col-title` or `nav a` respectively. To revert to the previous markup, set the `AppContext` switch to `false`:\r\n\r\n```csharp\r\nAppContext.SetSwitch(\"Microsoft.AspNetCore.Components.QuickGrid.EnableUrlBasedQuickGridNavigationAndSorting\", false);\r\n```\r\n\r\nAdditionally, when multiple `QuickGrid` components are used on the same page, each one now **must** have a unique `QueryParameterNamePrefix` value. Since `QueryParameterNamePrefix` defaults to `\"\"`, having two or more grids without explicitly setting different values will cause them to share the same query parameters (`page`, `sort`, `order`) for pagination and sorting, and interfere with each other. This applies to both SSR and interactive rendering.\r\n\r\n**Before (worked implicitly):**\r\n```razor\r\n<QuickGrid Items=\"@people\" Pagination=\"@pagination1\">...</QuickGrid>\r\n<QuickGrid Items=\"@cities\" Pagination=\"@pagination2\">...</QuickGrid>\r\n```\r\n\r\n**After (requires unique `QueryParameterNamePrefix` per grid):**\r\n```razor\r\n<QuickGrid Items=\"@people\" Pagination=\"@pagination1\">...</QuickGrid>\r\n<QuickGrid Items=\"@cities\" Pagination=\"@pagination2\" QueryParameterNamePrefix=\"cities\">...</QuickGrid>\r\n```\r\n\r\n### Shared `PaginationState` limitation\r\n\r\nEach `QuickGrid` propagates its page query parameter name to the associated `PaginationState` during `OnParametersSetAsync`, so that the connected `Paginator` uses the same query parameter name. This means **multiple `QuickGrid` components must not share the same `PaginationState` instance** if they have different `QueryParameterNamePrefix` values — the last grid to render will overwrite the query name on the shared state, causing the `Paginator` to read from the wrong query parameter. Each grid should have its own `PaginationState` instance.\r\n\r\n### Usage example\r\n\r\n```razor\r\n@using Microsoft.AspNetCore.Components.QuickGrid\r\n\r\n<QuickGrid Items=\"@people\" Pagination=\"@pagination\">\r\n    <PropertyColumn Property=\"@(p => p.PersonId)\" Sortable=\"true\" />\r\n    <PropertyColumn Property=\"@(p => p.FirstName)\" Sortable=\"true\" />\r\n    <PropertyColumn Property=\"@(p => p.LastName)\" Sortable=\"true\" />\r\n</QuickGrid>\r\n<Paginator State=\"@pagination\" />\r\n\r\n@* Multiple grids on the same page with different query parameter prefixes *@\r\n<QuickGrid Items=\"@cities\" Pagination=\"@pagination2\" QueryParameterNamePrefix=\"cities\">\r\n    <PropertyColumn Property=\"@(c => c.Name)\" Sortable=\"true\" />\r\n    <PropertyColumn Property=\"@(c => c.Country)\" Sortable=\"true\" />\r\n</QuickGrid>\r\n<Paginator State=\"@pagination2\" />\r\n\r\n@code {\r\n    PaginationState pagination = new PaginationState { ItemsPerPage = 10 };\r\n    PaginationState pagination2 = new PaginationState { ItemsPerPage = 5 };\r\n    private IQueryable<Person> people = GetPeople().AsQueryable();\r\n    private IQueryable<City> cities = GetCities().AsQueryable();\r\n}\r\n```\r\n\r\nFixes #51249\r\nFixes #57289\r\nFixes #66301","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dotnet/aspnetcore/issues/65451/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":1,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dotnet/aspnetcore/issues/65451/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null,"score":1.0}],"search_type":"lexical"}